  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday Night through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1108 AM CST Sun Nov 22 2026\n\nFor the forecast period, morning lows will stay in the 20s and 30s \nwith highs in the 50s. An inverted trough brings hope for more \nsubstantial rainfall to Middle Tennessee mid-week, but guidance is \nstill in disagreement about placement of the heaviest precipitation \nand amounts. More guidance is trending to leave the 65 corridor \nthirsty while watering the TN river area and the plateau, but not \neveryone agrees on this yet. We will have to continue to monitor \nrainfall amounts as we get more guidance in range in the coming \ndays, but hazardous weather risks remain low. Once this Thanksgiving \nsystem makes it through, weather will calm down for us, but the \npattern looks to remain active into the end of November.",
